--- A list of lists of numbers is a matrix where a tensor is taken, as a
--- list of rows that are tensors is: `tensor[rows]` and `stack[rows]` are
--- the matrix, `stack[rows, 1]` its columns stacked, ints as floats. Both
--- modes had stopped — the interpreter on "a list of array is not a list
--- of numbers", the compiled program not built — and `stack` of one had
--- reached the verifier as "the lowered program disagrees with itself".
use math
xs = push[push[[], 1.5], 2.5]
ys = push[push[[], 3.5], 4.5]
rows = push[push[[], xs], ys]
log[tensor[rows]]
log[stack[rows]]
log[stack[rows, 1]]
log[len[rows]]
ns = push[push[[], push[push[[], 1], 2]], push[push[[], 3], 4]]
log[tensor[ns] * 2.0]
--- rows of two lengths are no matrix: the program stops, saying so
ragged = push[push[[], push[push[[], 1.0], 2.0]], push[[], 3.0]]
log[stack[ragged]]
